3. AI Academic Topic Bot
To build an AI web application that is trained in the professors’ approved course information with different topics in different majors.
Professors begin the process of accumulating program or even “within program” shared knowledge (“canon”) – shared communal knowledge that is built collaboratively by a community of faculty that represents the “knowledge” parts of those programs learning goals – evolves over time
Students get different “topic bots” that reflect a lot of the shared knowing of the faculty in each topic… could be program specific, course sequence specific or even course specific. Ensures that the “knowledge exploration” (conversations) are “by design” from the faculty as starting point
Students get immediate answers while professors spend less time responding to repetitive emails.
The professor could also see: Top questions students asked this week. That could reveal where assignment instructions are unclear.
The school’s administrators can accumulate and put in the AI bot the domain knowledge, per program, in a way that can serve students, grow over-time, and develop community expertise.
--> Value Proposition: Instant student support. Effortless instructor insights. This AI web application acts as a secure, dual-purpose academic tool. By training exclusively on school professors’ verified materials from multiple majors, it provides students with immediate, accurate academic support in multiple topics while transforming student inquiries into actionable data to improve course design.
